{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nOperator decisions supersede this ticket's original framing (see its comments). **2026-08-10:** do\nNOT retune the fuzzy `low|medium|high` boundary — ordinal labels are an LLM anti-pattern, since\nmodels do not apply them reliably enough for deterministic gate behavior; replace the ladder with a\nclosed KIND set mapping deterministically to floor-vs-advisory in code. **2026-08-12:** do both\nhalves now — drop the inert-G5 hedge (no bump) AND land the conversion with its own\n`IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump (plan-v5). **C11 plan**\n(`reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/ordinal-migration-plan.md`, Phase 1): the plan-v5 batch is\n`undecomposed` + `dod_uncertifiable` together, plus the no-bump margin rider.\n\nEvidence, from this checkout's persisted REVIEW_RESULT sidecar corpus (22,503 plan findings carrying\n`verification.severity_attributes`). Every non-none grade on both axes floors impact to 0.85\n(`_PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_FLOOR` in `decide.py`), so `low` == `high`. `undecomposed` is graded 30 times;\nof all 30 bodies, 21 are \"this plan bundles N independently-releasable outcomes\" — a right-sizing\nobservation on an otherwise executable plan — yet each floors to 0.85 and 4 blocked.\n`dod_uncertifiable` is graded 1,413 times, mixing three distinct defects under one blind floor. Both\nprompts and the `undecomposed` description justify conservative grading by citing the deterministic\nG5 suppressor, but `veto_undecomposed_g5` fired ZERO times, so that hedge is inert. These are the\nlast ordinal override axes; `ORACLE_GRADE01` (plan-v3) and `DIVERGENCE_GRADE01` (plan-v4) are\nthe precedents to mirror.\n\n## What\n\n**Scope is ONE unit, not a bundle to split.** ADR 0054 section 4 requires impact-model shape changes\nto be batched behind one `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump, because each bump closes the current cohort.\nItems 2-3 are shape changes; 1 and 4 are no-bump riders that would otherwise be stranded from their\nevidence. The pieces are NOT independently releasable.\n\n1. **Prompt-hedge removal (no bump).** Delete the inert G5-suppressor hedge from both prompts and\n   the `undecomposed` description in `verify_models.py`.\n2. **`undecomposed` -> closed kind set (bump):** `none`; `bundles_separable_slices` — executable as\n   written but packs outcomes that could each ship alone, so splitting improves clarity only —\n   contributing `UNDECOMPOSED_BUNDLED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `missing_required_child` —\n   work the plan or its parent commits to has NO corresponding child/sibling — flooring;\n   `no_executable_breakdown` — no executable step sequence for its own scope, or an all-or-nothing\n   build whose riskiest unknown is never de-risked first — flooring.\n3. **`dod_uncertifiable` -> closed kind set (bump):** `none`; `underspecified_certification` — the\n   outcome IS certifiable and an oracle exists, but its exact command/path/assertion is not spelled\n   out — contributing `DOD_UNDERSPECIFIED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `uncertifiable_outcome` —\n   a committed outcome has NO acceptance criterion, test or proving mechanism at all — flooring;\n   `certification_cannot_prove` — a stated mechanism cannot establish the outcome (it names\n   something that does not exist or cannot detect what is claimed, or a trivially broken\n   implementation satisfies it) — flooring. NOTE: `impact_plan`'s amplifier forces `mult = 1.0` via\n   `_SEV01.get(\"dod_uncertifiable\")`, and `_SEV01` returns 0.0 for a kind name, so that force MUST\n   be rewritten against the new map or it silently stops firing.\n4. **Decision-margin telemetry (no bump).** Record `impact_sev - block_threshold` per finding in the\n   sidecar (C11 P0.2). Additive only.\n5. **Bump `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` plan-v4 -> plan-v5** in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`.\n\n**Evidence gate before landing (zero LLM).** Add\n`reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/plan_v5_rescore.py` re-scoring all 22,503 recorded findings\nunder the new maps and reporting old-vs-new flips; land rules and output under `docs/calibration/`.\nIt reads persisted `severity_attributes` as RAW dicts (never through the new `Literal` model, which\nwould reject the old labels) and maps each grade to a kind by documented rules. Per the R1\nbar, a lost block is UNJUSTIFIED iff the finding body describes a genuine gap (a committed outcome\nwith no/broken oracle, or missing required decomposition) yet re-maps to an advisory kind; any such\nflip means ESCALATE with the data, not land.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Add `UNDECOMPOSED_GRADE01` / `DOD_GRADE01` (+ CONTRIB constants and floor tuples) to `decide.py`\n   mirroring `ORACLE_GRADE01`; extend `_PLAN_GRADED_AXES` to all four graded axes and rewrite\n   `impact_plan`'s contributions, `has_override` and the amplifier force off `_SEV01`.\n2. Convert both fields in `verify_models.py` to `Literal` closed sets and rewrite both axis bullets\n   in the two verifier prompts; drop the hedge sentence in all three.\n3. Add the decision-margin field in `sidecar.py` and bump `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION`.\n4. In `tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py` REWRITE (not merely extend) the pre-existing cases keyed on\n   ordinal grades for these two axes — `test_hard_override_floors_low_axis_to_085`,\n   `test_each_ordinal_override_axis_triggers_floor`,\n   `test_dod_uncertifiable_forces_full_detection_weight` — to kind names, then add the new cases;\n   update `tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py`; pin the margin field in\n   `tests/unit/test_plan_review_sidecar.py`. `tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py`\n   pins the \"success criterion\" phrasing in the `dod_uncertifiable` bullet, so PRESERVE it.\n5. Write the re-score script; record rules + results in `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both axes are closed `Literal` kind sets. Verified:\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q -k literal` passes, asserting each field's\n      annotation holds the six kind names and none of `low`/`medium`/`high`.\n- [ ] Each advisory kind contributes 0.55 and never floors; each genuine-gap kind yields 0.85; both\n      CONTRIB constants sit strictly below the lowest blocking `block_threshold` (0.6) in\n      `plan_review/criteria_routing.json`, like `UNDERSPECIFIED_ORACLE_CONTRIB`; and the amplifier\n      still forces `mult = 1.0` for a non-none `dod_uncertifiable`. Verified:\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q` passes with cases pinning\n      `impact_plan({\"undecomposed\": \"bundles_separable_slices\"}) == 0.55`, the same for\n      `underspecified_certification`, 0.85 for the four gap kinds, the contrib-below-threshold\n      invariant, and a `self_revealing` + `underspecified_certification` finding at 0.55 not 0.44.\n- [ ] No prompt or field description cites the G5 suppressor. Verified:\n      `rg -n \"deterministic G5 signal already|signal already suppresses\" src/rebar/` exits 1.\n- [ ] The sidecar records a per-finding decision margin. Verified: `python -m pytest\n      tests/unit/test_plan_review_sidecar.py -q -k margin` passes.\n- [ ] `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` is `plan-v5`, batched per ADR 0054 section 4. Verified:\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py -q` passes, and the commit body\n      names the hedge removal, both conversions and the margin telemetry as riding one bump.\n- [ ] The re-score is landed and shows no unjustified lost blocks (rule above). Verified:\n      `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md` states the mapping rules and reports old-vs-new block\n      counts and the flip set; `python\n      reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/plan_v5_rescore.py` reproduces them.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n`make lint && make typecheck`, then `python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"decide or impact or\nverify_models or sidecar or criteria_vocabulary\"` and `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q -k\nplan_review`. The re-score is zero-LLM replay through the shipped compose functions, so no eval\nsuite is needed (ADR 0054). `veto_undecomposed_g5` removal and C11 Phase 2 are out of scope."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786508777788303001,"uuid":"53789c6e-6638-4ca7-9052-f5a582311f7c"}